      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there any chance the caller will want to handle different errors differently? `anyhow` is probably not the right choice for library error types, usually we define an enum or struct (with the help of `thiserror`) so that the caller can get information about them.",
      "revId": "32872ec2cb6d2785bbe9d68733c0e51d52f96aa1",
